    rationale: "Fraud rarely presents as one obvious falsehood; it presents as a pattern of small inconsistencies, and the correct response is to document, resolve with evidence, and escalate — not to proceed on the theory that no single item proves anything, confront the participant, or quietly withdraw and leave the next licensee to face the same file blind.",
